1.20.0: polajuice serve - the workspace on the native engine

polajuice serve [DIR] [--port N] is a small HTTP server inside the CLI
(POSIX sockets, loopback only, one request at a time with threaded
renders inside) that serves the workspace page and takes over its
rendering. The page probes /api/version on load; finding the native
engine it sends every render there instead of to the serial wasm, and
the header says so. What a local process adds: the folder's images in
the strip (raw ones as straight prints), exports written next to the
source with the recipe embedded, "apply to folder" batch runs, and
looks kept as looks/*.recipe files under the repo rather than in the
browser. Exports (NAME_camera.jpg) are recognized and left out of the
strip and of batches. A custom .cube loaded in the page still renders
in wasm, since the server has no file for it. Without a staged
web/films, the server builds the film manifest from data/luts, so a
fresh clone with 'make fetch-luts' has every stock in the dropdown.

src/cli/look.c holds the film/print resolution, compatibility checks
and recipe text as one Look, shared by the server; test_serve.sh
starts a server on a scratch folder and checks every endpoint, a
served render byte-identical to the CLI's render of the same look, a
dropped image in the body, export, batch skipping exports, looks as
files, and path-escape and bad-camera refusals. 'make serve' runs the
server (DIR=...).
